Off-by-one in LookupXPathKeyword: KeywordIndex is declared as
array[0..MaxHash-1], so index MaxHash is one past the end. The value read there
is interpreted as a TXPathKeyword and used to index the XPathKeywords pointer
array, which is then dereferenced.

All 48 real XPath keywords hash to 2..54, so tightening the bound loses none of
them; index 55 can only be produced by non-keyword tokens, for which xkNone is
the correct result.

--- a/packages/fcl-xml/src/xpathkw.inc
+++ b/packages/fcl-xml/src/xpathkw.inc
@@ -152,7 +152,7 @@
       else
         Exit;
   end;
-  if (hash >= 0) and (hash <= MaxHash) then
+  if (hash >= 0) and (hash < MaxHash) then
   begin
     p1 := XPathKeywords[KeywordIndex[hash]];
     if (ord(p1^) = Len) and
